From 59bd70991f9c70ca8ece03e07fe84537af76477d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jesus David Saavedra Latorre <iam.jesusd88@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:18:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/25] feat(dilemma): add Catppuccin Mocha RGB effect with
 subtle ripple to mac keymap

Add a custom RGB Matrix effect that paints the Catppuccin Mocha accent
palette as a gradient mirrored on both halves, scaled by the brightness
setting, plus a faint Lavender ripple (at most 22%, ~500 ms) on each key
press. Enable RGB_MATRIX_KEYPRESSES so the hit tracker runs; key presses
already reach both halves through SPLIT_TRANSPORT_MIRROR.

Make it the default mode at brightness 96 and bump the settings version so
an existing EEPROM switches to it once on the next boot.
---
